{"nodes": [{"id": "_xdrs__local_edrs_principles_001_success_probability_interpretation_policy", "label": "EDR-001: success_probability Interpretation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".xdrs/_local/edrs/principles/001-success-probability-interpretation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Judge prompts across modes interpreted success_probability inconsistently (author vs defense probability), producing wildly inconsistent results (5%, 50%, 85%) for the same case. Decision: success_probability always represents the AUTHOR's probability of winning (0-100), canonical in every mode; the display layer converts to the user's chosen side perspective. userSide/userPole/selectedMode must always be persisted together in Firestore to avoid partial-fallback side inversion on reload."}, {"id": "_xdrs__local_edrs_principles_001_success_probability_interpretation_success_probability_field", "label": "success_probability field", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".xdrs/_local/edrs/principles/001-success-probability-interpretation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_xdrs__local_edrs_principles_001_success_probability_interpretation_gemini_server_ts", "label": "gemini.server.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".xdrs/_local/edrs/principles/001-success-probability-interpretation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_xdrs__local_edrs_principles_001_success_probability_interpretation_app_tsx", "label": "App.tsx", "file_type": "code", "source_file": ".xdrs/_local/edrs/principles/001-success-probability-interpretation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_xdrs__local_edrs_principles_001_success_probability_interpretation_dbservice_ts", "label": "db